sm, resulting in elevated calcium levels in the blood (hypercalcemia). Additionally, adenomas in the pituitary gland can cause conditions such as Cushing's syndrome due to excessive production of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). Overall, adenomas are benign tumors that can have significant clinical implications depending on their location and the hormones they may affect.\",3\r\n5197,HORMONAS SEXUALES,\"HORMONAS SEXUALES, or sex hormones, are crucial hormones that regulate the development and functioning of reproductive organs. This group includes hormones such as FSH (follicle-stimulating hormone), LH (luteinizing hormone), and testosterone, as well as androgens and estrogens. The measurement of sex hormones is particularly important in clinical scenarios where there is a suspicion of adrenal carcinoma, as their secretion by a benign adenoma is quite rare. In cases of adrenal incidentalomas, where there is a clinical suspicion of malignancy, it is essential to evaluate the potential secretion of sex hormones by adrenal tumors. Thus, the assessment of these hormones plays a significant role in the diagnosis and management of conditions related to the adrenal glands and reproductive health.\",5\r\n3625,CARCINOMA SUPRARRENAL,\"Carcinoma suprarrenal is a rare primary malignant tumor that originates in the adrenal glands, with an incidence of approximately 1 in 1,000,000 inhabitants per year. This type of cancer is more commonly diagnosed in women and typically occurs in individuals between the ages of 40 to 50. Carcinoma suprarrenal may be suspected in cases of adrenal incidentalomas, which are unexpected findings of adrenal masses during imaging studies. Overall, carcinoma suprarrenal represents a significant concern in the context of adrenal cancer, highlighting the need for awareness and careful evaluation of adrenal masses.\",4\r\n4051,DEXAMETASONA,\"DEXAMETASONA, also known as dexamethasone, is a synthetic glucocorticoid and corticosteroid medication utilized i